<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105861" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῠλ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make knobby</i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόπαλα τετυλωμένα
			σιδήρῳ</span> clubs <i>knobbed</i> with iron, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.63
			</span></i>; of the outside of the 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίτριον, σκληρὸν καὶ τετ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					6.618
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>make callous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυλοῖ τὸ στόμα [ὁ χαλινός]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					6.9
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be made hard</i> or <i>callous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετυλωμένης τῆς μήτρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orib.
					22.7.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.10
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μακέλᾳ τετυλωμένος ἔνδοθι χεῖρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					16.32
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετυλωμένα βλέφαρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					5.99
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν χεῖρα καὶ τὴν ἀκοὴν πρὸς τὰ
					ἐξαρτήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>VP</u>
					26.118
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				2.18.9
			</span></i>.—Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυλωτός,</span> and 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυλόομαι.</span>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
